From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Mon, 24 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: control change and two-pass adjusts for more than two
 duelists

Adjust cases 3, 4 and 5 (processor.cpp) now test every duelist's set when n_duelists > 2.
In cases 4 and 5 the cards are grouped by the duelist that must control them (case 4: the
controller from refresh_control_status, stored when the set is filled; case 5: the owner).
get_control runs once per non-empty group, in turn order from the turn player. A card whose
target is not a living duelist goes to the Graveyard by rule. One static helper does both.

ControlAdjust (operations.cpp) uses two sides side_a and side_b (0 and 1 with two duelists,
else the two controllers with a non-empty set, in turn order). The receiving side chooses.
Case 3 moves a card to the other side, not opponent_of. More than two non-empty sets abort
in the YGO_N_TRAP build. Note: nothing in the core emplaces this process now (dead code).

TrapMonsterAdjust and ChangePos case 1 use a pass counter and a pass player when n > 2:
one pass per living duelist from the turn player or the reason player. The stock bool
oppo_selection and opponent_of stay in the n == 2 branch. TrapMonsterAdjust case 4 loops
once per living duelist when n > 2 (no duplicate visit after an elimination).

With two duelists every changed site takes the stock branch, so bytes and Lua call order
are the same. SwapControl needs no change (it uses the controllers of the cards); its
PLAYER_NONE line is left to T9. The pass player of ChangePos treats reason PLAYER_NONE
(2) as seat 2 until the sentinel task lands.

